  "notes": "DCM Shriram Ltd (NSE: DCMSHRIRAM) \u2014 diversified Indian agribusiness/industrial conglomerate. Three main segments: (1) Chloro-Vinyl (caustic soda, PVC, cement, power), (2) Sugar (4 plants in UP, ~38,000 TCD crushing capacity + ethanol distilleries + co-gen), (3) Agri-Inputs (Shriram Bioseed, Shriram Farm Solutions). Also Fenesta windows. Indian fiscal year ends March 31; FY24 = year ending Mar 2024. All values in INR millions (1 INR crore = INR 10 million; standard reported figures in crore are multiplied by 10). Source: annual reports filed with BSE/NSE, investor presentations on dcmshriram.com. Sugar segment heavily exposed to UP cane SAP and government ethanol blending policy. FY22-23 saw record results on chemicals + sugar tailwinds; FY24 weaker on chloro-vinyl downcycle and sugar margin compression; FY25 modest recovery. Sector classified as Diversified Agribusiness for comps. No primary land acreage carried \u2014 operations are processing/manufacturing-led. Figures rounded; not from machine-readable filings.",
